  "synthesis": {
    "description": "Prior month adjustment sheets are distributed to the scheduling and trading desks, who are asked to help clear them. Reviewers question individual items, such as why a counterparty change cut revenue or why a reduction in purchased energy produced a charge, and price revisions are explained back. Items needing deeper investigation are forwarded on, and the reviewer reports when most of the sheet is resolved while flagging items still open.",
    "steps": [
      "Distribute the prior month adjustment sheet and ask the desk to help clear it.",
      "Review each adjustment and question items that do not make sense.",
      "Explain price or volume revisions behind specific adjustments.",
      "Forward unclear items to the person best placed to investigate.",
      "Report the sheet as largely resolved and flag remaining open items."
    ],
    "approach": "Produce the adjustment sheet with a reason code and the underlying price or volume change attached to each line, so reviewers see why an item moved without asking. Track each line's status and owner until it is cleared.",
    "rationale": "Most of the mail is reviewers asking why an adjustment exists. A sheet layout with the cause and owner per line answers those questions up front and keeps open items visible.",
    "artifact_type": "template"
  },
